# API route documentation

Every new route must be recorded in `server/docs/api/`.

When you add or change a route in `RegisterRoutes`:

1. Add or update a markdown file under `server/docs/api/` (group by domain, e.g. `organization.md`).
2. Include method, path, auth requirement, and a working `curl` with a dummy raw JSON body when the endpoint accepts a body.

````markdown
## POST /api/v1/organization/create

Auth: required (JWT)

```bash
curl -X POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/organization/create \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer <token>" \
  -d '{"name":"Acme Corp"}'
```
````

```

No route ships without its docs entry.
```
